OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F431A1786551523
OL,3,CPeople line streets for glasses as
OL,4,CWales prepares for solar eclipse
OL,6,FPeople have been lining the streets
OL,7,Ffor viewing glasses as Wales prepares
OL,8,Fto watch the rare solar eclipse, with
OL,9,Fparts of the country named as some of
OL,10,Fthe best places to see it in the UK.
OL,12,FMore than 90% of the sun will be
OL,13,Fobscured by the moon between 18:00 and
OL,14,F20:00 on Wednesday (12 August).
OL,16,FThe event will be the fullest solar
OL,17,Feclipse visible from Wales since 1999,
OL,18,Fwith a spectacle of this scale not
OL,19,Fexpected again until 2081.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G1/6
